repository-code: "https://github.com/Oshoma123/botreg"
keywords:
  - dietary supplements
  - botanical adulteration
  - regulatory data
  - openFDA
  - GBIF
abstract: >
  BOTREG provides unified programmatic access to the United States public
  regulatory and label record for dietary supplements: the NIH Dietary
  Supplement Label Database, openFDA food enforcement, CAERS adverse event
  and drug enforcement endpoints, FDA warning letters, and California
  Proposition 65 sixty-day notices. It guards against three documented
  failure modes in those sources that return well-formed but wrong results.
  BAER, the Botanical Adulteration Event Record, is the derived dataset of
  regulatory events mentioning botanicals, annotated against the GBIF
  taxonomic backbone, with taxonomic match quality preserved rather than
  collapsed.
